    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d811">

                <pb facs="0706" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg694"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.24/257: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Turkey</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-04-20T19:00:00-04:00">April 20, 1942—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>157. Further to our cable 145 of April 10 [<hi rendition="#italic">14</hi>] with
                    particular reference to suggestion of enlarging existing Ankara Co-ordinating
                    Committee by United States representation, Department feels advisable that two
                    such representatives be provisionally designated at this time.</p>
                <pb facs="0707" n="695" xml:id="pg695"/>
                <p>You and the military attaché are so designated. War Department has given the
                    necessary approval for the latter. Any additional personnel will be left to your
                    discretion, as is also the authority to designate a member of your staff to
                    attend meetings on your behalf when desirable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
